ent\/SignalBatchStrategy","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" over a stream of the unit’s one value, made afresh"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"for each iteration."}]}],"kind":"content"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The unit’s work runs in the signal’s task each time iteration begins; a unit that fails","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"ends the batched sequence with its error. When the batched sequence ends first, the unit’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"work is cancelled; a unit whose work ignores cancellation keeps the batch’s internal task","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"alive until it returns, though the batched sequence itself ends at once. A","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SingleValueSubject","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" takes ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/documentation\/Afluent\/SignalBatchStrategy\/signal(_:)-7c9kk","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" instead, which","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves the subject alone. Each batched sequence iterated with this strategy runs the unit","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"anew and fires once when it completes.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Example","level":2,"text":"Example"},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let reachable = DeferredTask { try await server.waitUntilReachable() }","for try await requests in outbox.batch(strategy: .either(.count(20), .signal(reachable))) {","    try await send(requests)","}"]}],"kind":"content"}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"abstract":[{"text":"Flushes once, when the given unit of work completes.","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Afluent\/docume